  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Kasino (Finnish). See rules.objective and rules.gameplay for details.',
    Player: "Kasino (Finnish Casino) is the most popular fishing card game in Finland. Unlike standard Casino, it uses 'Royal' capture values (J=11, Q=12, K=13) and features a unique 'In-Hand Value' system where Aces and the two Kasino cards (10D and 2S) have higher values when held in the hand than when on the table. It is a game of calculation, memory, and defensive stalling.",
    objective: 'Capture cards to score points. The first player to reach 16 points wins the match.',
    gameplay: "1. Match: Play a card from hand to capture any group of cards on the table whose values sum to the hand card's value.\n2. Building: In the Finnish variant, direct building is less common than in English Casino; capture by sum is the primary mechanic.\n3. **MÃ¶kki**: If you clear the entire table, you score 1 point immediately (turn the card face-up in your pile).",
    keyRules: [
      'Play one card from hand per turn; capture by same value or by sum of table cards; captures are not compulsory.',
      'Ace counts 1 on table, 14 from hand; cannot capture a single Ace.',
      '2 of Spades (Small Kasino): 2 on table, 15 from hand. 10 of Diamonds (Big Kasino): 10 on table, 16 from hand.',
      'Sweep (mökki): clearing the table scores 1 point; card placed face up in capture pile. If all players have a sweep, they cancel.',
      'No sweep points after the last deal; no sweep points if any player has 10 or more.',
      'First to 16 points wins. Aces and Kasino points awarded when captured; game can end mid-hand. Tiebreak: Aces and Kasino first, then spades, then cards.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
